## Setup Procedure

**Important: Set up from downstream to upstream (against traffic flow). This ensures you are always working behind protection.**

{% if is_flagger %}
1. Identify both {% if is_afad %}AFAD{% else %}flagger{% endif %} station positions (do not staff yet — stations are staffed after all devices are in place, step 7): Station #1 at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(flagger_station_1_ft) }} ft (approach side, 100 ft upstream of the taper start, closed-lane side); Station #2 at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(flagger_station_2_ft) }} ft (opposing approach, 300 ft past the work-area end per CDOT S-630-1 Case 17).
{% elif is_near_intersection %}
1. Position arrow board at the upstream start of the merging taper (station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_start_station) }} ft), centered in the closed right lane. Set to LEFT ARROW mode (traffic merges left, out of the closed lane). Activate flashing.
{% else %}
1. Position arrow board at the upstream start of the shoulder taper (station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_start_station) }} ft). Set to RIGHT ARROW mode (for right shoulder closure). Activate flashing.
{% endif %}

2. Place the END ROAD WORK sign (G20-2) at the downstream termination (station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(end_sign_station_ft) }} ft), right side of road {{ "{:.0f}".format(sign_offset_ft) }} ft from centerline.{% if is_divided %} Place matching sign on left side.{% endif %}{% if is_flagger %} Place the opposing-direction G20-2 past the upstream end of the work zone (left side).{% endif +%}

{% if is_flagger %}
3. {% if num_ds_cones > 0 %}Place {{ num_ds_cones }} traffic cones in the downstream taper, between station -{{ "{:,.0f}".format(ds_taper_len_ft) }} ft (right lane edge) and station 0 (centerline) at {{ "{:.0f}".format(ds_spacing_ft) }} ft spacing — this taper returns right-direction traffic from the centerline back to the right lane edge past the work area (MUTCD §6B.08 ¶12; S-630-1 Case 17 annotates the run 100' MAX.). Then place{% else %}Place{% endif %} {{ num_tangent_cones }} traffic cones along the centerline boundary between the open opposing lane and the closed work lane at {{ "{:.0f}".format(tangent_spacing_ft) }} ft spacing, starting at station 0 (downstream end of work zone) and working upstream to station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(params.work_zone_length_ft) }} ft.
{% elif is_near_intersection %}
3. {% if ni_extend_to_corner %}Run the closed-lane cone line from the upstream curb line of the cross street (station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ni_upstream_curb_ft) }} ft, past the downstream end of the work zone) up to station 0 — {{ num_ds_cones }} traffic cone{% if num_ds_cones != 1 %}s{% endif %} at approximately {{ "{:.0f}".format(ds_spacing_ft) }} ft spacing. The closure extends to the corner and the lane reopens beyond the intersection; place no devices inside the intersection itself, curb line to curb line (MUTCD Fig. 6P-21 / S-630-1 Case 18). Then place{% elif num_ds_cones > 0 %}Place {{ num_ds_cones }} traffic cones in the downstream reopening taper, between station -{{ "{:,.0f}".format(ds_taper_len_ft) }} ft (lane edge) and station 0 (lane line) at {{ "{:.0f}".format(ds_spacing_ft) }} ft spacing — this taper returns traffic into the reopened right lane past the work zone (MUTCD §6B.08 downstream taper). Then place{% else %}Place{% endif %} {{ num_tangent_cones }} traffic cones along the closed-lane line through the work zone at {{ "{:.0f}".format(tangent_spacing_ft) }} ft spacing, starting at station 0 (downstream end of work zone) and working upstream to station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(params.work_zone_length_ft) }} ft. Offset: {{ "{:.0f}".format(ni_lane_line_offset_ft) }} ft from centerline.{% if ni_companion_cones > 0 %} Then continue the closed-lane cone line upstream from the work zone to the downstream curb line of the cross street (station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ni_downstream_curb_ft) }} ft), and again from the upstream curb line (station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ni_upstream_curb_ft) }} ft) up to the taper — {{ ni_companion_cones }} cones total, with no devices inside the intersection itself. The lane must already be closed where it crosses the intersection (MUTCD §6N.12.12).{% endif +%}
{% else %}
3. {% if num_ds_cones > 0 %}Place {{ num_ds_cones }} traffic cones in the downstream taper, between station -{{ "{:,.0f}".format(ds_taper_len_ft) }} ft (shoulder edge) and station 0 (lane edge) at {{ "{:.0f}".format(ds_spacing_ft) }} ft spacing — this taper returns traffic from the lane edge back to the shoulder edge past the work zone (MUTCD §6B.08 downstream taper). Then place{% else %}Place{% endif %} {{ num_tangent_cones }} traffic cones along the right lane edge at {{ "{:.0f}".format(tangent_spacing_ft) }} ft spacing, starting at station 0 (downstream end of work zone) and working upstream to station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(params.work_zone_length_ft) }} ft. Offset: {{ "{:.0f}".format(lane_edge_offset_ft) }} ft from centerline.
{% endif %}

4. Place G20-5P WORK ZONE plaque(s) within the work zone at approximately {{ "{:,.0f}".format(plaque_interval_ft) }} ft intervals.{% if is_divided %} Place matching plaques on left side.{% endif +%}

{% if is_flagger %}
5. Place {{ num_taper_drums }} channelizing drums in the one-lane two-way taper, starting at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_end_station) }} ft and working upstream to station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_start_station) }} ft. Space drums at {{ "{:.0f}".format(taper_spacing_ft) }} ft intervals (approximately 20 ft per MUTCD §6B.08 — this taper stages stopped traffic behind the flagger; it must be short enough to not be mistaken for a transition). Drums transition from the right lane edge ({{ "{:.0f}".format(lane_edge_offset_ft) }} ft) to the centerline (0 ft).
{% elif is_near_intersection %}
5. Place {{ num_taper_drums }} channelizing drums in the merging taper, starting at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_end_station) }} ft and working upstream to station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_start_station) }} ft. Space drums at {{ "{:.0f}".format(taper_spacing_ft) }} ft intervals. Drums transition from the lane edge ({{ "{:.0f}".format(lane_edge_offset_ft) }} ft) to the lane line ({{ "{:.0f}".format(ni_lane_line_offset_ft) }} ft), closing the right lane.
{% else %}
5. Place {{ num_taper_drums }} channelizing drums in the shoulder taper, starting at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_end_station) }} ft and working upstream to station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(taper_start_station) }} ft. Space drums at {{ "{:.0f}".format(taper_spacing_ft) }} ft intervals. Drums transition from the lane edge ({{ "{:.0f}".format(lane_edge_offset_ft) }} ft) to the shoulder edge ({{ "{:.0f}".format(shoulder_edge_offset_ft) }} ft).
{% endif %}

6. Place advance warning signs upstream of the taper:
{{ advance_signs_setup_bullets }}
{% if is_divided %}
   Place matching signs on left side at each location.
{% endif %}
{% if is_flagger %}
   Repeat the series for the opposing approach (left side, negative stations — S-630-1 Case 17: "SIGN SEQUENCE IS THE SAME FOR OPPOSITE DIRECTION").

7. Staff both {% if is_afad %}AFAD{% else %}flagger{% endif %} stations{% if is_afad %} (position and activate the AFADs; the operator must maintain sight of both devices){% else %} (STOP/SLOW paddles, high-visibility apparel, radio or agreed hand-signal communication between stations){% endif %}{% if is_night %}, with station flood lighting per S-630-1 Sheet 2 Note 22{% endif %}. Verify each station is visible to approaching traffic from the full advance-warning distance and has an identified escape path. Begin the alternating one-way operation.
{% endif %}
{% if is_near_intersection %}

7. Place the mainline regulatory and bookend signs, single side, {{ "{:.0f}".format(sign_offset_ft) }} ft from centerline: R2-10 BEGIN DOUBLE FINES ZONE at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ni_r2_10_station_ft) }} ft (half the C spacing inside the outermost W20-1, per S-630-1 Case 18); G20-1 at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ni_g20_1_station_ft) }} ft; R2-11 END DOUBLE FINES ZONE at station {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ni_r2_11_station_ft) }} ft (downstream, past the lane reopening).

8. Place the cross-street advance sets — one set per approach leg. Stations for each set are measured along that leg FROM the intersection curb line, increasing away from the intersection:
{% for ap in ni_approaches %}
   - **{{ ap.id }} approach** ({{ ap.speed_mph }} mph, {{ ap.road_type_human }}): W20-1 ROAD WORK AHEAD at {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ap.w20_1_ft) }} ft and R2-10 BEGIN DOUBLE FINES ZONE at {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ap.r2_10_ft) }} ft, both on the approach side {{ "{:.0f}".format(ap.sign_offset_ft) }} ft from that road's centerline — the W20-1 sits at twice the key distance A, the R2-10 at A, where the S-630-1 Sheet 10 advance-signing key gives A = {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ap.a_dist_ft) }} ft for this leg's own speed and road type. R2-11 END DOUBLE FINES ZONE at {{ "{:,.0f}".format(ap.r2_11_ft) }} ft on the departure side (facing traffic leaving the intersection).{% if ap.signalized %} This approach is signalized: signal operation must be reviewed before work begins (MUTCD §6N.12; Part 4) — see the audit trail.{% endif +%}
{% endfor %}

**Sequencing note:** The MUTCD does not prescribe the order of mainline versus cross-street setup. Whether the cross-street sets go up before, after, or interleaved with the mainline sequence is the Traffic Control Supervisor's determination for this site.
{% endif %}

## Takedown Procedure

{% if is_flagger %}
**Important: The one-lane operation ends before its warning signs come down. Flaggers control traffic until the roadway is fully restored to two-way operation.**

1. Complete work and clear all personnel and equipment from the work area.
2. Under continued flagger control, remove the work-zone cones and the taper drums (restoring the closed lane).
3. Cease the alternating one-way operation and release both {% if is_afad %}AFAD{% else %}flagger{% endif %} stations.
4. Remove advance warning signs on both approaches: {{ takedown_sign_sequence }}.
5. Remove G20-5P plaques and the G20-1/G20-2 BEGIN/END ROAD WORK signs.
{% else %}
**Important: Remove from upstream to downstream (with traffic flow). Remove advance warning signs first, work zone devices last.**

1. Remove advance warning signs: {{ takedown_sign_sequence }}.{% if is_divided %} Remove both sides at each station.{% endif +%}
2. Remove taper drums from upstream to downstream.
3. Deactivate and remove arrow board.
4. Remove work zone cones from upstream to downstream.
5. Remove G20-5P plaques.
6. Remove G20-2 END ROAD WORK sign(s).
{% if is_near_intersection %}
7. Remove the mainline R2-10 / R2-11 DOUBLE FINES ZONE pair and the G20-1 sign.
8. Remove each cross-street advance set (W20-1, R2-10, R2-11 per approach). The order of mainline versus cross-street takedown is the Traffic Control Supervisor's determination.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

## Safety Notes

- All personnel in the work zone must wear ANSI Class 2 (daytime) or Class 3 (nighttime) high-visibility apparel.
{% if is_night -%}
- Nighttime operation: Ensure all devices meet retroreflectivity requirements. Flagger stations require 500W quartz illumination at minimum 8 ft height per CDOT S-630-1 Sheet 2 General Note 22.
{% endif -%}
{% if is_divided -%}
- Divided highway: All warning and regulatory signs must be posted on BOTH sides of the roadway per CDOT S-630-1 Sheet 2 General Note 8.
{% endif -%}
{% if rightmost_lane_assumed -%}
- Closed lane: this plan draws the closure on the RIGHTMOST lane. That is a modeling assumption, not an MUTCD rule — the work location dictates the lane. If the work occupies a different lane, this plan does not apply as drawn.
{% endif -%}
- Maintain {{ "{:.0f}".format(buffer_space_ft) }} ft longitudinal buffer space between the taper and the work area at all times.
- Maximum speed reduction per sign installation: 15 mph (CDOT S-630-1 Sheet 2 General Note 3).
- This plan was generated by MHT Tool. A certified Traffic Control Supervisor (TCS) must review, approve, and sign before field implementation.
- Reference: CDOT S-630-1, MUTCD 11th Edition Part 6, Colorado Supplement (effective January 18, 2026).

